    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABK2mxzQ",
      "title": "feat(template): add OPCMUpgradeV900",
      "author": "ZakAyesh",
      "number": 1591,
      "body": "Adds `OPCMUpgradeV900`, the upgrade half of the v9 (interop) release: it calls `OPContractsManagerV2.upgradeSuperchain` once, then `upgrade` per chain, so a set of chains already on op-contracts/v8 steps onto the v9 OPCM.\n\n**Ordering:** this task runs before the `OPCMMigrateV900` task in #1582. `migrate` requires every chain to already be on the v9 OPCM.\n\nDifferences from `OPCMUpgradeV800`, all driven by the v9 OPCM:\n- The only permitted upgrade instruction is `overrides.cfg.startingRespectedGameType`; the `startingAnchorRoot` override is rejected, so the anchor-root inputs are gone and the super-root anchor is carried forward. `_validate` asserts the respected game type landed and the anchor was not cleared.\n- Version gate accepts any 9.x and checks `isPermittedUpgradeSequence` per chain.\n- SUPER_CANNON_KONA is enabled when the factory already carries it (v8 cleared the CANNON_KONA impl it used to key off).\n- `Challenger` is read with a tolerant lookup: super-game-only chains register none.\n\n**Example task and simulation.** `sep/045-opcm-upgrade-v900` (Unichain Sepolia + OP Sepolia) simulates against the throwaway v9 OPCM (9.0.5) Andrea deployed on Sepolia on 2026-10-22 for template testing (`0xe09c417496c786abffefa676da9e11aab2c32ea9`, not an rc, no tag, no registry entry). The simulation passes end to end at fork block 11999987 with no validator errors for either chain. A real task must point at the released v9 OPCM. The example is not skipped in `simulate-all-templates`, so CI depends on that throwaway contract staying deployed; happy to add a skip like #1582 if preferred.\n\nSetup tests: `test/template/OPCMUpgradeV900Setup.t.sol` (5 tests, Sepolia fork).\n\nOpen for review: the prestate in the example is the chains' current SUPER_CANNON_KONA prestate as a placeholder, and the ZK game path is unsupported as in V800.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-26T19:21:28Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 689,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABHa1AFQ",
      "title": "sep/112-114: OP Sepolia OPE key rotation (batcher, proposer, unsafe signer)",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1568,
      "body": "OP Sepolia OP Enterprise key rotation in three tasks, sequenced by the Q4 multisig ceremonies calendar. sep/112 sets the OPE batcher (`0x64EDa4F93314ECd619bd4f79D8d1F8112A4E6e16`) and sep/114 the OPE unsafe block signer, both with `SetBatcherAndOrSigner` from the Sepolia FoundationUpgradeSafe; sep/113 rotates the `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) proposer on the OP Sepolia DisputeGameFactory to `0x9884C33C65111DA7Bbed0e63cD2392F503b135F5` with `SetDisputeGameArgs`, signed by the L1PAO (impl, anchorStateRegistry and zero bond kept live). The batcher and signer are split so the signer can rotate later (Oct 30) than the batcher and proposer (Oct 15).\n\nBlocking: the OP Sepolia SystemConfig owner is today the EOA `0xfd1D2e729aE8eEe2E146c033bf4400fE75284301`, not the FoundationUpgradeSafe. It has to `transferOwnership` to the FoundationUpgradeSafe outside this repo before sep/112 and sep/114 can execute; until then both configs override `SystemConfig.owner()` (slot `0x33`) for simulation, same pattern as the Unichain/Soneium batcher tasks. The OPE unsafe block signer in sep/114 is the `0xdead00000000000000000000000000002002dead` placeholder.\n\nNonce pins follow sep/110-111 (Unichain Sepolia): sep/112 FUS 79, sep/113 L1PAO 58 / FUS 80 / SC 72, sep/114 FUS 81. sep/115 is left free for U21 Sepolia (Nov 9), and Soneium Minato moves to sep/116-118 (#1565, now stacked on this PR). Calldata re-derived with `cast` in the docs, and `just simulate-stack` passes with the VALIDATION.md hashes on both signing paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T21:13:21Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-26T18:05:58Z",
      "additions": 193,
      "deletions": 0
    },
